  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "40270610",
      "title": "Optimizing React with MillionJS",
      "sourceHash": "83a63f4859432153c3530bf8d5c4d26f3c8639d1cc7f20c54e4a9933a5662944",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.57,
          "end": 3.75,
          "en": "So that was a lot about component functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.75,
          "end": 8.28,
          "en": "state, the virtual DOM and all these important things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.28,
          "end": 10.38,
          "en": "But, therefore, at this point you now have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.38,
          "end": 14.34,
          "en": "a super-detailed understanding of how React works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.34,
          "end": 17.703,
          "en": "and how you can optimize React in certain parts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.87,
          "end": 22.77,
          "en": "To conclude this section, I now wanna introduce you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.77,
          "end": 25.44,
          "en": "to another package that you can also use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.44,
          "end": 29.91,
          "en": "to optimize the performance of your React applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.91,
          "end": 33.06,
          "en": "and that's the Million.js package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.06,
          "end": 35.22,
          "en": "A rather strange name for sure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.22,
          "end": 37.713,
          "en": "but a package that's really interesting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.73,
          "end": 40.56,
          "en": "If you search for Million.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.56,
          "end": 42.36,
          "en": "you should find its official page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.36,
          "end": 44.94,
          "en": "and you can learn more about the package there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.94,
          "end": 46.89,
          "en": "and you most importantly learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.89,
          "end": 49.62,
          "en": "that it can make React faster.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.62,
          "end": 53.55,
          "en": "They advertise with up to 70% at the point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.55,
          "end": 55.5,
          "en": "of time where I'm recording this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.5,
          "end": 59.13,
          "en": "And you can use this package absolutely for free,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.13,
          "end": 60.84,
          "en": "just to be clear.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.84,
          "end": 63.9,
          "en": "Now, you can learn more about this package if you dive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.9,
          "end": 66.6,
          "en": "into the official docs and you can learn more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.6,
          "end": 70.23,
          "en": "about all its different configuration options here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.23,
          "end": 74.03999999999999,
          "en": "to squeeze out all the possible performance gains,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.03999999999999,
          "end": 78.84,
          "en": "but you can also get started by using it in automatic mode.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.84,
          "end": 82.28999999999999,
          "en": "And when using that mode, adding it to a project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.28999999999999,
          "end": 84.15,
          "en": "and improving the performance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.15,
          "end": 87.39,
          "en": "of your project is really simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.39,
          "end": 91.2,
          "en": "You just have to install it into your project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.2,
          "end": 93.63,
          "en": "So here I'll quit my development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.63,
          "end": 97.38,
          "en": "and run npm install million on CodeSandbox.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.38,
          "end": 99.963,
          "en": "You would simply add it to your dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.61,
          "end": 106.17,
          "en": "And then here, since this is a Vite-based project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.17,
          "end": 110.22,
          "en": "you have to go to the vite.config file and tweak that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.22,
          "end": 113.25,
          "en": "Though the official docs give you details",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.25,
          "end": 116.88,
          "en": "on how to integrate Million.js into different projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.88,
          "end": 119.78999999999999,
          "en": "created with different popular tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.78999999999999,
          "end": 122.43,
          "en": "for creating React projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.43,
          "end": 125.01,
          "en": "Here you have Vite, but for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.01,
          "end": 128.643,
          "en": "also Create React App which is a popular alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.08,
          "end": 133.56,
          "en": "Now, when using Vite as we do, you can basically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.56,
          "end": 137.91,
          "en": "copy this code here and replace the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.91,
          "end": 140.373,
          "en": "in this vite.config file with that code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.87,
          "end": 143.57999999999998,
          "en": "And that's all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 143.57999999999998,
          "end": 146.31,
          "en": "With that you enabled Million.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.31,
          "end": 149.67000000000002,
          "en": "and whilst you might not get all possible improvements out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.67000000000002,
          "end": 151.71,
          "en": "of this library just by doing that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 151.71,
          "end": 155.04,
          "en": "you should get some improvements out of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.04,
          "end": 158.01,
          "en": "So now if you restart the development server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.01,
          "end": 161.1,
          "en": "and especially if you would build the application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 161.1,
          "end": 163.65,
          "en": "for production and you would deploy it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.65,
          "end": 166.47,
          "en": "something we'll also cover in this course, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.47,
          "end": 169.23,
          "en": "you should get a better performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 169.23,
          "end": 172.44,
          "en": "Though at least here I'm actually getting an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 172.44,
          "end": 174.96,
          "en": "which can be fixed though by going",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 174.96,
          "end": 179.07,
          "en": "to these icon components and ignoring them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 179.07,
          "end": 181.8,
          "en": "as instructed here in the instructions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.8,
          "end": 183.483,
          "en": "on the Million.js website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 184.98,
          "end": 188.25,
          "en": "I can simply add this comment in front",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 188.25,
          "end": 192.24,
          "en": "of my component function to ignore it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 192.24,
          "end": 195.3,
          "en": "and opt out of these Million.js improvements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 195.3,
          "end": 196.803,
          "en": "for this component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 197.97,
          "end": 202.5,
          "en": "And if I do that and reload, now the app renders again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 202.5,
          "end": 206.55,
          "en": "and it works and behaves as before, as you can tell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 206.55,
          "end": 210.3,
          "en": "This all works fine without errors in the console",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 210.3,
          "end": 213.57,
          "en": "and now technically it should be faster.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 213.57,
          "end": 217.38,
          "en": "Of course for this demo app, this doesn't really matter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 217.38,
          "end": 220.53,
          "en": "and would be pretty hard to measure, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 220.53,
          "end": 224.79,
          "en": "because it already is a pretty basic fast app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 224.79,
          "end": 227.88,
          "en": "But if you are working on a more complex project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 227.88,
          "end": 231.72,
          "en": "and in there you maybe have parts where you are outputting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 231.72,
          "end": 234.57,
          "en": "and updating a lot of interactive data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 234.57,
          "end": 238.77,
          "en": "Million.js might be able to speed up that application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 238.77,
          "end": 241.62,
          "en": "And I absolutely recommend diving deeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 241.62,
          "end": 245.28,
          "en": "into the official docs to learn how you can configure it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 245.28,
          "end": 248.37,
          "en": "in greater detail and how you can use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 248.37,
          "end": 252,
          "en": "to squeeze out every last piece of performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 252,
          "end": 255.93,
          "en": "Because in the end, Million.js improves the performance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 255.93,
          "end": 260.07,
          "en": "by replacing React's virtual DOM mechanism",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 260.07,
          "end": 262.65,
          "en": "with a more efficient mechanism,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 262.65,
          "end": 267.45,
          "en": "which is faster and derives required DOM updates faster",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 267.45,
          "end": 270.753,
          "en": "than the existing algorithm that's built into React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 271.8,
          "end": 275.28,
          "en": "And that's why I wanted to introduce you to Million.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 275.28,
          "end": 278.1,
          "en": "as part of this section, because even though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 278.1,
          "end": 280.08,
          "en": "we don't need it for this project here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 280.08,
          "end": 282.09000000000003,
          "en": "you might be able to benefit from it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 282.09000000000003,
          "end": 283.983,
          "en": "in your future projects.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
